# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Pages (HTML) must always revalidate, so a content change, like swapping the
# seasonal banner from Oktoberfest to Christmas, shows up straight away instead
# of being served from a stale browser cache. Without this, returning visitors
# can keep seeing an old page for days.
#
# Our CSS / JS / images all carry a ?v=YYYYMMDD cache-buster in their URL, so
# those are safe to cache hard and forever (a new ?v= simply fetches a fresh
# copy). Data files (catalog.json, meta.json) have no ?v=, so they fall under
# the revalidate rule below and stay fresh too.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Versioned, effectively immutable assets (the ?v= query busts them on change).
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/logo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
